
================================================================================================
PART 0 -- GAUGE FIXING, BACKGROUND, AND THE APPROXIMATION SCHEME (stated, not hidden)
================================================================================================
  [SETUP] Unitary gauge T = t.  This uses up the time reparametrisation completely; the khronon is eaten and there is no Stueckelberg field left.
  [SETUP] Residual symmetry after T = t: time-dependent spatial diffeomorphisms x^i -> x^i + xi^i(t,x).  Scalar part xi^i = d^i xi.
  [SETUP] General scalar spatial metric h_ij = e^{2psi} delta_ij + 2 d_i d_j E.  Under the residual scalar diffeo, (traceless part of) E shifts by -2 xi, so E can be set to ZERO.  GAUGE FIXED: h_ij = e^{2 psi} delta_ij.
  [SETUP] Leftover residual freedom: xi with d_i d_j xi - (1/3) delta_ij d^2 xi = 0, i.e. xi linear in x -- global translations/dilatation-free rigid maps.  These act trivially on a plane wave of finite k.  So (phi, B, psi) with N = e^{phi}, N_i = d_i B, h_ij = e^{2 psi} delta_ij is a COMPLETE and NON-REDUNDANT scalar parametrisation.  [DERIVED from the transformation law]
  [SETUP] phi is DEFINED as delta ln N (not delta N).  a_i = D_i ln N is then EXACT and linear in phi, which removes a spurious quadratic tadpole term.
  [BG] Background: flat spatial slice, N^(0) with a^(0)_i = q n_i = q zhat CONSTANT.
  [BG] Then D_i a^(0)_j = d_i a^(0)_j - Gamma^k_ij a^(0)_k = 0 - 0 = 0, so T^(0)_ij = 0 EXACTLY and Y_a^(0) = 0.  [DERIVED]
  [ASSUMED] FROZEN-BACKGROUND / EIKONAL SCHEME.  ln N^(0) = q z means N^(0) = e^{qz}: an envelope.  Different terms of the ADM Lagrangian carry different powers of N^(0), so we evaluate the quadratic form at the point z = 0 (N^(0) -> 1) while keeping a^(0)_i = q exactly.  No derivative ever acts on the envelope in the terms that matter: a_i = d_i ln N is envelope-exact, and D_i D_j (q z) = 0 identically.  The dropped corrections are relative O(q/k) = O(sqrt(X0) a0/(k c^2)).
  [ASSUMED] TADPOLE.  The uniform-acceleration background is not a vacuum solution; it is sourced.  Terms proportional to the background field equations are k-INDEPENDENT (they multiply the O(e^2) parts of the fields with no derivatives), so they can only contaminate the k^0 sector.  We therefore quote the omega^2, k^2 and k^4 coefficients, which are tadpole-free, and DO NOT quote k^1 or k^0 coefficients.
  [SCHEME] Accuracy: EXACT in X0 and in (lam_K, eta_K, eps); leading order in q/k.  Kept: {omega^2, k^2, eps k^4}.  Dropped: everything relative O(q/k).

================================================================================================
PART 1 -- BACKGROUND AND THE FIRST-ORDER TIDAL TENSOR (k || a^(0), the clean case)
================================================================================================
  [ok]   X^(0) = q^2 = X0 exactly
  [ok]   Y_a^(0) = 0 exactly  (T^(0)_ij = 0 on a uniform-acceleration, flat-slice background)
  [ok]   Y_a^(1) = 0 exactly  (Y_a is quadratic in delta T; no linear-order Y term at all)
         => the ENTIRE quadratic Y-contribution is -2 eps A(X0) delta T_ij delta T^ij, with A evaluated on the background.  No F_XY cross term at this order.
  [ok]   delta T_ij = u (n_i n_j - delta_ij/3) with u = phi'' - 2 q psi'   [independent hand check]
         hence  Y_a^(2) = (2/3)(phi'' - 2 q psi')^2 .  The phi'' piece is the FOURTH-derivative hazard: it is second spatial derivatives of the LAPSE, squared.
  [DERIVED] In Fourier (k || zhat):  u -> -(k^2 A_phi + 2 i q k A_psi), so
  [DERIVED]   Y^(2) -> (2/3)[ k^4 |phi|^2 + 4 q^2 k^2 |psi|^2 + O(q k^3) cross ].
  [DERIVED]   * k^4 |phi|^2 : the lapse hazard.        * 4 q^2 k^2 |psi|^2 : an O(eps A X0) shift of the scalar gradient term -- the exact scalar analogue of the tensor sector's dc_T^2/c^2 = 2 eps A X0.

================================================================================================
PART 2 -- CANONICAL STRUCTURE: WHAT IS NON-DYNAMICAL
================================================================================================
  [ok]   Y_a contains NO time derivatives (pi^ij is exactly the (lam_K-)GR momentum)
  [ok]   X contains NO time derivatives
  [ok]   Y_a contains NO shift B (momentum constraint H_i is exactly the (lam_K-)GR one)
  [ok]   d(Y-sector)/d(psi-dot) = 0 identically (no new momentum from the tidal term)
  [DERIVED] So the Gen-2 tidal operator adds only SPATIAL derivatives.  phi and B remain non-dynamical; the phase-space count is unchanged from Gen-1: (20 - 12 - 2)/2 = 3 = 2 tensor + 1 khronon.  No Ostrogradsky partner appears from the (d^2 phi)^2 term because phi carries no time derivative at all.

